Symbiknow
Alternative: connect a stdio MCP agent
Use a long-lived stdio session. Substitute your actual absolute project path:
```
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "symbiknow": {
      "command": "/Users/benreich/Projects/symbiknow/.venv/bin/python",
      "args": ["-m", "app.server"],
      "cwd": "/Users/benreich/Projects/symbiknow",
      "env": {
        "SYMBIKNOW_DATA_DIR": "/Users/benreich/Projects/symbiknow/data"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Only one server may own a data directory. Each MCP client host has its own message limits; SDK interoperability does not establish the limits of every agent host. Base64 is present in protocol responses. The CLI suppresses it in printed download summaries, but the host must control what enters the agent's context.
